{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-30T18:10:18.622Z","data":{"text":"I've completed the task. Here's a summary of what I did and why.\n\n## What the task asked\nDelete `osq done` (sources, registration, tests), add `tests/done-removed.test.ts`, and leave the `done_manual` event, `[manual]` squash line, report manual counts, and doctor's check untouched.\n\n## The blocker I hit\nThe watcher's git guard (`src/watcher/git-guard.ts` → `scopeViolations`) resolves the task `scope` with `resolveScope`, which returns `absolutePath: null` for an exact-declared path that no longer exists. The guard filters those out, so **every deleted in-scope file is reported as a `scope_violation` and kills the task**. Attempt 2 died exactly this way. Task 2 hit the same bug and the accepted resolution was inert stub modules.\n\n## What I did\n- Reduced `src/cli/done.ts`, `src/core/lifecycle/done.ts`, and `tests/done-manual.test.ts` to inert `export {}` modules (matching task 2's precedent).\n- Removed the `doneCommand` import and `done <id> <task>` registration from `src/cli/index.ts` (nothing else).\n- Removed the two `done throws` cases from `tests/command-error-changes.test.ts` only.\n- Removed the `markTaskDoneManual` import and the manual-done case from `tests/worktree-lifecycle.test.ts` only.\n- Added `tests/done-removed.test.ts`: no `done` command registered, unknown `done` invocation exits non-zero and writes no marker, and the command modules export no done entry points.\n\n## Verification\n- `node --import tsx --test tests/done-removed.test.ts` → 3 pass, exit 0\n- `pnpm verify` → typecheck, UI typecheck, build, full test suite, and lint all pass\n- All changed files are inside the task `scope`; only the result file is outside it.\n\nThe deviation (inert stubs instead of deletion, and the adapted third assertion) is documented under `## Deviated`, `## Missing context`, and `## Outside scope` in `.run/results/4.md`."}}
